Subject: [PATCH 3/3] refactor(likelihood): extract
 rectangular_excitation_compensator (eq. 14 specialized: exponential temporal
 mass on min(T - t_j, w), Gaussian rectangle mass eq. 27) and rewire
 Itot_excite onto it; pure lift, op order preserved. The atom is named and
 documented for what it computes -- NOT the general-domain compensator:
 non-rectangular domains overcharge (declared approximation), and finite
 spatial_window remains event-side only (documented discrepancy). Unit tests:
 independent SciPy erf reference, finite gradients w.r.t. (alpha, beta,
 sigmax_2), window>=horizon untruncated recovery (I8b at atom level).
 test_identities.py's I11 helper now assembles background + the production
 atom (per review: the atom keeps its own independent-reference unit test so
 the conservation test does not share an unverified formula with the code
 under test; the traced-Itot_txy guard is retained). Verified: ruff clean;
 29/29; value AND gradient pins bit-identical.

